  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=\\{-2,2\\}\\times {N}_{0}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is either $-2$ or $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is a natural number or zero.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in \\{-2,2\\},\\,y\\in {N}_{0}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-2$ and whose $y$-coordinate  is any natural number or zero.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-2}=\\{(-2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {N}_{0}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14191646/assets/4418001fb8fb44cc5cd35b258136ee696d35d27198549177a2f60a7297d31bb1.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate  is any natural number or zero.\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {N}_{0}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14191646/assets/bf74df976235b72a24047e2ec27aad7d426b6ceb1fcb948bc656b77bf0635911.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $\\{-2,2\\}\\times {N}_{0}$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14191646/assets/e1df54a171c531d9417cde85d559ad852e0761931d23b0f23aadbdd562f51743.png)",
